    {
      "id": "qd-KzveGGtL33SztQW7pO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 400.4581179525559,
      "y": 30647.227810174078,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#d0bfff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 260432426,
      "version": 595,
      "versionNonce": 96807449,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1780638291043,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We have some technologies that helps\nus to make these kind of queuing\ninfrastructure.\nEx -> Redis, RabbitMQ these provide\nlike published and subscriber kind\nof data.\nwe can handle queue overflowing\nusing Horizontal scaling.\nlike AWS SQS is able to support\n3000 request per second.\nRedis support atmost one, means\nonly 1 processor can pickup payload\nIn Redis and RabbitMQ once one processor\nload payload from queue that payload is\nremoved from queue.\nif we dont want this we can use Kafka.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We have some technologies that helps\nus to make these kind of queuing\ninfrastructure.\nEx -> Redis, RabbitMQ these provide\nlike published and subscriber kind\nof data.\nwe can handle queue overflowing\nusing Horizontal scaling.\nlike AWS SQS is able to support\n3000 request per second.\nRedis support atmost one, means\nonly 1 processor can pickup payload\nIn Redis and RabbitMQ once one processor\nload payload from queue that payload is\nremoved from queue.\nif we dont want this we can use Kafka.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
